     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">HI everybody<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I was trying to run this line of the physignal function:<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">plot(PS.shape$PaCA, phylo = TRUE)<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">But I got one error plus several warnings <span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">Error in plot.window(...) : need\r\nfinite &#39;xlim&#39; values<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">In addition: Warning messages:<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">1: In min(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to min; returning Inf<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">2: In max(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to max; returning -Inf<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">3: In min(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to min; returning Inf<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">4: In max(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to max; returning -Inf<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">5: In plot.window(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I used this line with the corresponding xlim and ylim values\r\n<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">plot(PS.shape$PaCA, phylo = TRUE, xlim=c(-0.1,0.1),\r\nylim=c(-0.1,0.1))<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">but I got these warnings:<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Warning messages:<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">1: In plot.window(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">2: In plot.xy(xy, type, ...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">3: In axis(side = side, at = at,\r\nlabels = labels, ...) :<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\"><span> \r\n</span>&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">4: In axis(side = side, at = at,\r\nlabels = labels, ...) :<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\"><span> \r\n</span>&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">5: In box(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">6: In title(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I tried to use the geomorph dataset (plethspecies) with plot(PS.shape$PaCA,\r\nphylo = TRUE)<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">but I got exactly the same error, can somebody tell me where\r\nthe error is? Is this related to my geomorph version (3.1.2)? BTW, I\r\nsuccessfully obtained summary(PS.shape)and plot(PS.shape)<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Thanks!!<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Paolo<br></div></div><div><br> <table style=\"border-top:1px solid #d3d4de\">\r\n\t<tr>\r\n      <td style=\"width:55px;padding-top:18px\"><a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=link&amp;utm_campaign=sig-email&amp;utm_content=webmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dlink%26utm_campaign%3Dsig-email%26utm_content%3Dwebmail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484284169000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0u5HAWZKJC1iuplTMElq_I\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/IAkhl6EbYbQYD9J_1Dc6N_HPU5Z488DnGcKcnWpOKuYmchAYVxkuaNLcLza-a4lma2s9ti4CdivC6ngcOg6DxsKIfQSj1jUPE23T-RPW6SSIBxsEZEVz9o7f4AeRul4zwq6JNmxjsa05TVZzHfERYYI-=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ipmcdn.avast.com/images/icons/icon-envelope-tick-round-orange-animated-no-repeat-v1.gif\" alt=\"\" width=\"46\" height=\"29\" style=\"width:46px;min-height:29px\"></a></td>\r\n\t\t<td style=\"width:470px;padding-top:17px;color:#41424e;font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">Libre de virus. <a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medi