     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Pablo,<div><br></div><div>I was able to get the same error as you but it worked fine if the code was changed to:</div><div><br></div><div>plot(PS.shape$<b>PACA</b>, phylo = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>A key difference is that I am using version 3.3.1, installed from Github.  We did indeed have a $PaCA object in the previous version (3.3.0) that we have since changed as a result of Phylogenetically-aligned Component Analysis being changed to Phylogenetically Aligned Component Analysis, using the acronym, PACA, as a result of the review process for our recently accepted paper.  I suspect that the problem is you are using a help file that does not correspond to the version of geomorph you are using because neither $PaCA nor $PACA were part of the physignal output in version 3.1.2.  You would get the same error trying to plot an object that does not exist, e.g., plot(PS.shape$<a href=\"http://this.is.sure.to.work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://this.is.sure.to.work&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484284173000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0pRZ9rgi_akWtlNEbzAxp7\">this.is.sure.to.work</a>, phylo = TRUE).</div><div><br></div><div>You might consider making sure you are using a help file with the same version (at the bottom of the help file) as the geomorph version you are running.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Mike <br><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
