     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Pablo,<div><br></div><div>I was able to get the same error as you but it worked fine if the code was changed to:</div><div><br></div><div>plot(PS.shape$<b>PACA</b>, phylo = TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>A key difference is that I am using version 3.3.1, installed from Github.  We did indeed have a $PaCA object in the previous version (3.3.0) that we have since changed as a result of Phylogenetically-aligned Component Analysis being changed to Phylogenetically Aligned Component Analysis, using the acronym, PACA, as a result of the review process for our recently accepted paper.  I suspect that the problem is you are using a help file that does not correspond to the version of geomorph you are using because neither $PaCA nor $PACA were part of the physignal output in version 3.1.2.  You would get the same error trying to plot an object that does not exist, e.g., plot(PS.shape$<a href=\"http://this.is.sure.to.work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://this.is.sure.to.work&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484284176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw232yRGFqzJc8DoKtevyTDk\">this.is.sure.to.work</a>, phylo = TRUE).</div><div><br></div><div>You might consider making sure you are using a help file with the same version (at the bottom of the help file) as the geomorph version you are running.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Mike <br><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Nov 1, 2020, at 11:02 AM, Pablo Fisichella &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fisiche...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">HI everybody<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I was trying to run this line of the physignal function:<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">plot(PS.shape$PaCA, phylo = TRUE)<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">But I got one error plus several warnings <span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">Error in plot.window(...) : need\r\nfinite &#39;xlim&#39; values<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">In addition: Warning messages:<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">1: In min(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to min; returning Inf<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">2: In max(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to max; returning -Inf<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">3: In min(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to min; returning Inf<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">4: In max(x) : no non-missing\r\narguments to max; returning -Inf<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">5: In plot.window(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I used this line with the corresponding xlim and ylim values\r\n<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">plot(PS.shape$PaCA, phylo = TRUE, xlim=c(-0.1,0.1),\r\nylim=c(-0.1,0.1))<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">but I got these warnings:<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Warning messages:<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">1: In plot.window(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">2: In plot.xy(xy, type, ...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">3: In axis(side = side, at = at,\r\nlabels = labels, ...) :<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\"><span> \r\n</span>&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">4: In axis(side = side, at = at,\r\nlabels = labels, ...) :<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\"><span> \r\n</span>&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">5: In box(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,112,192)\">6: In title(...) :\r\n&quot;phylo&quot; is not a graphical parameter<span></span></span></p><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span> </span><br></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I tried to use the geomorph dataset (plethspecies) with plot(PS.shape$PaCA,\r\nphylo = TRUE)<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">but I got exactly the same error, can somebody tell me where\r\nthe error is? Is this related to my geomorph version (3.1.2)? BTW, I\r\nsuccessfully obtained summary(PS.shape)and plot(PS.shape)<span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;line-height:115%;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Thanks!!<span></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Paolo<br></div></div><div><br> <table style=\"border-top:1px solid rgb(211,212,222)\">\r\n\t<tbody><tr>\r\n      <td style=\"width:55px;padding-top:18px\"><a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=link&amp;utm_campaign=sig-email&amp;utm_content=webmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dlink%26utm_campaign%3Dsig-email%26utm_content%3Dwebmail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484284176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RCVVOAkcNhRG-F3ZQWiiR\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/IAkhl6EbYbQYD9J_1Dc6N_HPU5Z488DnGcKcnWpOKuYmchAYVxkuaNLcLza-a4lma2s9ti4CdivC6ngcOg6DxsKIfQSj1jUPE23T-RPW6SSIBxsEZEVz9o7f4AeRul4zwq6JNmxjsa05TVZzHfERYYI-=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ipmcdn.avast.com/images/icons/icon-envelope-tick-round-orange-animated-no-repeat-v1.gif\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:46px;min-height:29px\" width=\"46\" height=\"29\"></a></td>\r\n\t\t<td style=\"width:470px;padding-top:17px;color:rgb(65,66,78);font-size:13px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">Libre de virus. <a href=\"https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=link&amp;utm_campaign=sig-email&amp;utm_content=webmail\" style=\"color:rgb(68,83,234)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.avast.com/sig-email?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dlink%26utm_campaign%3Dsig-email%26utm_content%3Dwebmail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484284176000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RCVVOAkcNhRG-F3ZQWiiR\">www.avast.com</a> \t\t</td>\r\n\t</tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n<a width=\"1\" height=\"1\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a></div><div><br></div>\